<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <data noupdate="0">

        <!--
            Operational cash intake is a BILLING concept, so the group that
            authorizes it lives here, in the module that owns the receipt,
            the allocation and the payment wizard.

            It was previously declared in yoya_reception_bridge. That could
            never work as the authorization boundary: yoya_reception_bridge
            DEPENDS ON hospital_billing, so this module can neither reference
            the group in its own ACLs nor name it in its Python guards without
            a circular dependency, and has_group() on an xmlid belonging to
            an uninstalled module raises. The group is re-homed here by
            migrations/18.0.1.5.0/pre-migrate.py, which re-points the existing
            ir.model.data row so current members are preserved.

            Deliberately implies nothing. Taking money and registering patients
            are separable duties: a cashier is not a receptionist, and a
            receptionist is not a cashier.
        -->

        <record id="group_hospital_cashier" model="res.groups">
            <field name="name">Hospital Cashier</field>
            <field name="category_id" ref="hospital_management.module_category_hospital_management"/>
            <field name="comment">Records operational payment receipts and allocates them
                against charges. Deliberately implies neither Receptionist nor Accountant,
                so taking money and registering patients can be separated duties. Holds no
                accounting authority: applying an advance, refunding, and posting to
                accounting remain with the Accountant and above.</field>
        </record>

        <!--
            INSURANCE / CREDIT OFFICER.

            Declared here for the same structural reason as the cashier group:
            the Python guards that enforce it live in hospital_billing
            (models/payer_agreement.py), and a group declared downstream cannot
            be named by an upstream guard without a dependency cycle.

            IMPLIES NOTHING, deliberately. Specifically NOT:
              hospital_billing.group_hospital_cashier          (no cash intake)
              hospital_management.group_hospital_accountant    (no posting)
              hospital_management.group_hospital_manager       (no activation)
              hospital_management.group_hospital_receptionist
              yoya_reception_bridge.group_hospital_front_desk_nurse

            WHAT IT GRANTS (security/ir.model.access.csv):
              hospital.payer            read / write / create
              hospital.payer.agreement  read / write / create / unlink

            WHAT IT CANNOT DO, and where that is enforced:
              activate / suspend / resume / expire / supersede / terminate an
                                        agreement
                                        payer_agreement.ACTIVATION_GROUPS, checked
                                        in _assert_state_transition() on EVERY
                                        write path, not only in the buttons
              edit an active agreement's terms
                                        payer_agreement.FROZEN_TERM_FIELDS in
                                        write(); no context key lifts it
              delete a non-draft agreement
                                        payer_agreement.unlink()
              record an operational payment
                                        hospital_billing OPERATIONAL_INTAKE_GROUPS
                                        (charge_line.py): group absent
              post accounting           assert_invoice_authorized
                                        (hospital_billing_accounting): group absent
              read patient cash amounts groups=OPERATIONAL_MONEY_READ on the money
                                        fields: group absent

            Preparing commercial terms and committing the hospital to them are
            separable duties. That separation is the entire reason this group
            exists rather than widening the Accountant.
        -->

        <record id="group_hospital_insurance_officer" model="res.groups">
            <field name="name">Hospital Insurance / Credit Officer</field>
            <field name="category_id" ref="hospital_management.module_category_hospital_management"/>
            <field name="comment">Maintains payer master data and drafts payer agreements.
                Deliberately implies no other role. Holds NO activation authority: bringing
                an agreement into force, suspending it or terminating it is reserved to the
                Hospital Manager and System Administrator. Holds NO cash-intake authority and
                NO accounting authority.</field>
        </record>

    </data>
</odoo>
